{
  "info": {
    "name": "Healthcare Realtime Vitals Lakehouse",
    "description": "Live HTTP endpoints of the healthcare-realtime-vitals-lakehouse project, running against the Floci AWS emulator. Import this file in Postman (Import > Upload Files). Endpoint defaults below already point at the running local stack.\n\nFolders:\n- Patients API (L3): API Gateway -> Lambda -> DynamoDB on Floci.\n- Trino REST: submit SQL over HTTP (what the trino CLI does).\n- Superset API: login + dashboard reads.\n- AWS via SigV4 (advanced): Floci emulates AWS as plain HTTP; Postman's AWS Signature auth signs requests like boto3 does.\n\nTip: run `make seed` before the latest-vitals requests so seeded readings exist for P0001-P0004.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "patients_api",
      "value": "http://patients.execute-api.localhost.floci.io:4566",
      "type": "default"
    },
    {
      "key": "trino_base",
      "value": "http://127.0.0.1:8083",
      "type": "default"
    },
    {
      "key": "trino_user",
      "value": "trino",
      "type": "default"
    },
    {
      "key": "superset_base",
      "value": "http://127.0.0.1:18088",
      "type": "default"
    },
    {
      "key": "floci_endpoint",
      "value": "http://127.0.0.1:4566",
      "type": "default"
    },
    {
      "key": "aws_region",
      "value": "us-east-1",
      "type": "default"
    },
    {
      "key": "aws_access_key",
      "value": "test",
      "type": "default"
    },
    {
      "key": "aws_secret_key",
      "value": "test",
      "type": "default"
    },
    {
      "key": "patient_id",
      "value": "P0001",
      "type": "default"
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Patients API (L3) - API Gateway -> Lambda -> DynamoDB on Floci",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "GET /patients/{id}/alerts",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{patients_api}}/patients/{{patient_id}}/alerts",
              "host": ["{{patients_api}}"],
              "path": ["patients", "{{patient_id}}", "alerts"]
            },
            "description": "Alerts for a patient from the DynamoDB `alerts` table. Expect 200 with a JSON list (may be empty)."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "GET /patients/{id}/latest-vitals",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{patients_api}}/patients/{{patient_id}}/latest-vitals",
              "host": ["{{patients_api}}"],
              "path": ["patients", "{{patient_id}}", "latest-vitals"]
            },
            "description": "Latest normalized reading per patient (DynamoDB `latest_vitals`). Needs seeded fixtures: run `make seed`. Without data returns a business 404: {\"error\": \"no latest vitals for P0001\"} - a valid negative test."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "POST /patients/{id}/latest-vitals (negative - method not allowed)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{patients_api}}/patients/{{patient_id}}/latest-vitals",
              "host": ["{{patients_api}}"],
              "path": ["patients", "{{patient_id}}", "latest-vitals"]
            },
            "description": "Only GET routes exist on this API. Expect HTTP 404 (method not allowed) - exercises route-level behaviour."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "GET /patients/{id} (404 when route/data absent)",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{patients_api}}/patients/{{patient_id}}",
              "host": ["{{patients_api}}"],
              "path": ["patients", "{{patient_id}}"]
            },
            "description": "Expect {\"message\":\"Not Found\"} unless this route is defined in infra/modules/apigateway/main.tf."
          },
          "response": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Trino REST - SQL over HTTP",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "POST /v1/statement - count vitals",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "X-Trino-User",
                "value": "{{trino_user}}"
              },
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "text/plain"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "SELECT count(*) AS vitals_rows FROM iceberg.healthcare.vitals",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "sql"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{trino_base}}/v1/statement",
              "host": ["{{trino_base}}"],
              "path": ["v1", "statement"]
            },
            "description": "Initiates a Trino query. The response carries columns + a `nextUri` you follow with GET requests to page results - the doc says: loop GET on nextUri (with X-Trino-User) until the request has a `data` array with the answer. Works exactly like the trino CLI under the hood."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "GET {nextUri} - resume/step a query",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "X-Trino-User",
                "value": "{{trino_user}}"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{next_uri}}",
              "host": ["{{next_uri}}"]
            },
            "description": "After POSTing a statement, copy the returned `nextUri` into the {{next_uri}} variable and GET it to fetch result pages."
          },
          "response": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Superset API",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "POST /api/v1/security/login - get access token",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\"username\":\"admin\",\"password\":\"admin\",\"provider\":\"db\",\"refresh\":true}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{superset_base}}/api/v1/security/login",
              "host": ["{{superset_base}}"],
              "path": ["api", "v1", "security", "login"]
            },
            "description": "Returns an access_token. A test script stores it for the requests below.",
            "event": [
              {
                "listen": "test",
                "script": {
                  "exec": [
                    "const json = pm.response.json();",
                    "if (json.access_token) { pm.collectionVariables.set('superset_token', json.access_token); }"
                  ],
                  "type": "text/javascript"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "GET /api/v1/dashboard/1 - Vitals Live dashboard",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Authorization",
                "value": "Bearer {{superset_token}}"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{superset_base}}/api/v1/dashboard/1",
              "host": ["{{superset_base}}"],
              "path": ["api", "v1", "dashboard", "1"]
            },
            "description": "Metadata for the provisioned 'Vitals Live' dashboard (id 1). Run the login request first."
          },
          "response": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "AWS via SigV4 (advanced - Floci emulates AWS over plain HTTP)",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "POST Kinesis.ListStreams (X-Amz-Target signed)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/x-amz-json-1.1"
              },
              {
                "key": "X-Amz-Target",
                "value": "Kinesis_20131202.ListStreams"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{floci_endpoint}}",
              "host": ["{{floci_endpoint}}"],
              "path": []
            },
            "description": "Same wire call boto3 makes. Use Postman's 'AWS Signature' auth preset with {{aws_access_key}}/{{aws_secret_key}}/{{aws_region}} and service `kinesis`, then it returns the real ListStreams JSON. Do this AFTER the login request if you set collection variables from scripts.",
            "auth": {
              "type": "awsv4",
              "awsv4": [
                {
                  "key": "accessKey",
                  "value": "{{aws_access_key}}",
                  "type": "string"
                },
                {
                  "key": "secretKey",
                  "value": "{{aws_secret_key}}",
                  "type": "string"
                },
                {
                  "key": "region",
                  "value": "{{aws_region}}",
                  "type": "string"
                },
                {
                  "key": "service",
                  "value": "kinesis",
                  "type": "string"
                }
              ]
            }
          },
          "response": []
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}